---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/blogs.css';
---

<Layout title="Engineering Work — Safu" description="Selected backend, AI, machine learning, and quantitative engineering projects by Safu Harry.">
	<main class="blog-page">
		<Nav />

		<header class="blog-hero">
			<div class="blog-hero__identity">
				<img src="/IMG-20210808-WA0072.jpg" alt="Safu Harry" loading="eager" />
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Engineering Journal · Open Source · Architecture</p>
					<h1>Systems built to be <span>reused.</span></h1>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p>
				Selected engineering work across backend architecture, AI systems, machine learning, and quantitative
				development. The focus is not only on applications, but on building software foundations that can be extended,
				tested, packaged, and reused.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="project-grid" aria-label="Selected projects">
			<article class="project-card project-card--featured">
				<div class="project-card__meta">
					<span>01 · Open Source Python Library</span>
					<span>v0.1.0 · Published</span>
				</div>
				<h2>FastApiBackbone</h2>
				<p class="project-card__lede">
					A reusable backend foundation for Python services built around FastAPI. Rather than treating FastAPI as the
				entire backend architecture, FastApiBackbone supplies the surrounding infrastructure required to build durable
					applications: environment-driven configuration, asynchronous SQLAlchemy, database lifecycle management,
					Alembic migrations, structured logging, health probes, and a reusable application factory.
				</p>

				<div class="project-card__callout">
					<strong>Now available as a Python package.</strong>
					<span>Installable distribution · semantic versioning · automated build and release workflow</span>
				</div>

				<div class="project-card__architecture">FastAPI → API composition → application services
					↓
				configuration + lifecycle + structured logging
					↓
				SQLAlchemy 2.x ↔ PostgreSQL / SQLite
					↓
				Alembic migrations</div>

				<div class="project-card__tags">
					<span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>SQLAlchemy 2.x</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>SQLite</span><span>Alembic</span><span>Pydantic</span><span>structlog</span><span>Async I/O</span><span>PyPI</span>
				</div>

				<div class="project-card__actions">
					<a class="project-card__link" href="https://github.com/safuh/FastApiBackbone" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source →</a>
					<a class="project-card__link" href="https://pypi.org/project/fastapi-backbone/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on PyPI →</a>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="project-card">
				<div class="project-card__meta"><span>02 · AI Systems</span><span>Active Development</span></div>
				<h2>PAssist</h2>
				<p class="project-card__lede">
					A provider-agnostic AI platform built around the same backend engineering principles. PAssist combines a
					modular FastAPI service with identity and JWT authentication, persistent conversations, AI provider
					abstraction, local Ollama integration, retrieval, tools, memory, and extensible domain boundaries.
				</p>
				<div class="project-card__architecture">Identity → JWT authentication → sessions
					↓
				FastAPI application → domain modules
					↓
				AI provider contract → Ollama / compatible APIs
					↓
				SQLAlchemy 2.x → Alembic → PostgreSQL</div>
				<div class="project-card__tags">
					<span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>JWT</span><span>Argon2</span><span>SQLAlchemy</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Ollama</span><span>LLMs</span><span>RAG</span><span>Tool Calling</span>
				</div>
				<a class="project-card__link" href="https://github.com/safuh/Passist" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore PAssist →</a>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section class="engineering-note" aria-labelledby="note-title">
			<p class="eyebrow">The engineering philosophy</p>
			<h2 id="note-title">Infrastructure first. Domain second.</h2>
			<p>
				FastApiBackbone is the reusable infrastructure substrate: asynchronous application structure, database lifecycle,
				migrations, configuration, logging, health checks, and clean extension points. It is deliberately domain-neutral
				so that another Python service can adopt the foundation without inheriting assumptions from a particular product.
			</p>
			<p>
				PAssist demonstrates the next layer: a concrete application domain built with identity, security, AI provider
				abstraction, conversations, tools, knowledge retrieval, and memory. Together, the projects show the progression
				from reusable backend infrastructure to a complex AI-enabled application.
			</p>
		</section>

		<footer class="footer">
			<Footer />
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>
